  "text": "Vaccination began in the late 18th century when Edward Jenner used cowpox to protect against smallpox, creating the first modern vaccine. The 19th century work of Louis Pasteur led to vaccines for radies and later for anthrax, establishing the principle of using weakened or killed microbes to induce immunity. In the early 1900s, the diphtheria toxoid and the polio inactivated vaccine dramatically reduced deaths from these diseases. The mid -20th century saw the development of the measles, mumps, and rubella MMR combined vaccine, and the widespread rollout of the polio -oral vaccine, which nearly eradicated polio worldwide. The World Health Organization launched the expi -",
